{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nA colleague witnessed the driver lose consciousness and fail to respond for 12 seconds during a break, and the current physician referral explicitly records a blackout with the mechanism under investigation; although the driver recalls heat, hunger and a racing heartbeat beforehand, neither syncope, seizure nor hypoglycaemia has been confirmed, cardiac monitoring is pending, and uncertainty about a remote dizzy spell does not erase the documented recent event.\n\nThe employer's copied form relates to an earlier period of work and contains a broad satisfactory box without the measurements underlying it, whereas the current nurse entry identifies the source of each specific finding; the driver's wish to continue scheduled duties is recorded as a preference, not as proof that the present assessment has resolved the documented concern.\n\nFor the occupational reviewer, the nurse retains both the definite findings and the limitations of the available account, including the timing and testing conditions where they matter, rather than producing a single reassuring label; the driver is told which information is on file and which details still require confirmation, without replacing the recorded clinical evidence with an employer's preference.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
